## Authentication

The provider accepts two credentials. Most resources and data sources need an Admin API key. The service account ones (`anthropic_service_account`, `anthropic_service_accounts` and `anthropic_service_account_workspace_member`) only accept an OAuth bearer token. Set both to manage everything from one provider block.

### Admin API key

Create an Admin API key in the [Anthropic console](https://console.anthropic.com/settings/admin-keys), then set `api_key` or the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable.

### OAuth bearer token

Before running Terraform, log in with the `ant` CLI under a dedicated profile with the `org:admin` scope (see [Admin access](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/cli/authentication#admin-access)), then export its access token:

```shell
ant auth login --profile admin --scope "org:admin"
export ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=$(ant auth print-credentials --profile admin --access-token)
```

You can also pass the token to `auth_token` in the provider block.

